{
  "doc": "M3-C05-02 story (act1_ch05.md B07-B10) on env-art's Ashcrown kit in its own frame since M3-ENV-1303 (ADR 0200; tools/act1/ch05_ashcrown_dressing.py, which wrote these points once and writes the collision and the dressing): the pilgrims' causeway from StairFoot up to the forecourt, the flying stair (48°, HeroStairs: ADR 0193) to the crown (tier 6, y 42), the trial down the east ambulatories of tiers 6 to 3 (t1-t4: release, gates, bowl, catch-rod running north; the east vein stairs (60°) down, chained by Stair_t<k> until the strike reaches the tier below), and the anvil court in the anvil hall (floor y -4: the anvil at z -8.4, the Matron's alcove on the west wall, Kahre's door at the crater loggia). The walk down ends at tier 3's east vein stair, whose head is the anvil_court trigger. The outer pilgrim stair runs north (x 0, z 0 to -88: the Tenders' gate A01, the grave tier A02, the copper tier A03) to the crown platform (z -88 to -100), where the crown pavilion and the catch-spire stand. The four inner tiers run back south along x 40 (t1 the crown, t2 to t4 below it), each with a catch-rod, a copper bowl (Bowl_<tier>), its vein-gates (blocks named for the trial's gates; the view turns them), floor plates on t4, and a release lever; Stair_<tier> walls the way down until the strike reaches that tier. The sealed side vein (QuenchSeal) and the quench-trough alcove are off tier 3's east wall. The anvil court is at the mountain's foot (z 0 to 14), with the anvil-stone, the Matron's alcove, the sea-facing arch and Kahre's chamber door. Random fights on the outer stair only (none in the trial, none in the court). trial_view: the stage actor shown on the tier-4 plates and the charged bowl's light (white-violet: lightning is never glimmer's gold, cyan or teal). Env-art's Ashcrown kit replaces the blocks.",
